#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544994} :activity/id #uuid "e5d016ea-97f9-5f7e-b3aa-b53ea168f095" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049335 :topic/id #uuid "ecb1b06f-16f7-5312-9cad-31f797ed7b6f" :topic/math-academy-id 1287} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544903 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d62d2e68-5eee-5bc7-afa4-c823d3717d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{50}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544543}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544543} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d21ebbf-1121-50e2-8b37-00e70a6f94e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "58e03782-f890-5578-a853-4a903526c725" :question/math-academy-id "q-280718" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,2,k⟩$, $b=⟨-3,0,4⟩$, and $c=⟨2,-1,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0\\cdot 5-4\\cdot (-1))-2((-3)\\cdot 5-4\\cdot 2)+k((-3)\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =4-2(-15-8)+3k \\\\  & =50+3k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 50+3k & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{50}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{50}{3}.$"} :step/id #uuid "0d92669c-e2e2-524a-a056-94858ce6f069" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544945}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544920 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4745fa01-7267-5d7d-80a7-da776c08b11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458758} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6770d3-5bd6-55b6-b578-032b42984508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458815} {:answer/id #uuid "87767553-4117-55d5-ab34-eebfa1e2b999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458866} {:answer/id #uuid "9b91be34-01c4-5335-b541-f723bc434b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458902} {:answer/id #uuid "9e493727-fb30-528b-be73-42746650771c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458905}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186458758} :answer-field/id #uuid "cffe9ad2-0939-5976-9d7b-05a76872555a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5208cfc4-b7ed-5787-b174-631ca841e3f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128486" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(8,0,5),$ $B(8,-3,3),$ $C(5,2,5),$ and $D(7,-1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(8i-3j+3k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-3,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(5i+2j+5k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-3i+2j \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(7i-j+4k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+3((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =9-10 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-1|=1.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3e712f71-5132-5fc8-9220-1c4e12fc44db" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544903}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544939 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d62eb44-4e3a-5892-a344-22adca5fb4b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339674} {:answer/id #uuid "44264ce2-e3a9-5eee-be94-e13b2e0593c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339727} {:answer/id #uuid "4f8808dc-6f23-5a33-9124-c4c4fa2dbcf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339852} {:answer/id #uuid "c947e433-5802-530f-8f38-59049f701448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340912} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f27876-a2cf-5204-a145-b4f7fba572a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341314}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340912} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac0fe630-b555-5ba6-bee4-4141e867e478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed1f88a5-7f29-5728-a62d-81ac2d1ace51" :question/math-academy-id "q-73753" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(-2,1,1)$, $B(2,1,0)$, $C(1,-1,2)$, and $D(3,-2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =4i-k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j-2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =5i-3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨5,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot (-3))-0-(3\\cdot (-3)-5\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =36-1 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|35|=35.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7180c506-8977-5256-a014-4e1e049c02cf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544920}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544945 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153692ac-17dc-5340-8ab8-c764df7ca660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293019}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293019} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b34c4d0-3f40-5fab-a961-3f1c1324f59d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "61f3e6a0-31a0-537c-a9de-e6c7ae59826e" :question/math-academy-id "q-280722" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,2⟩$, and $c=⟨2,k,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (b\\times c)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ k & 5\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot k)-3(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2)=(20-2k)+12 \\\\  & =32-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 32-2k & =0 \\\\ -2k & =-32 \\\\ k & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=16.$"} :step/id #uuid "7c03e152-dc69-5f79-b833-63b638ead8ee"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544994 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544855 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f4b5ae5-dd42-5130-a079-3437f957abdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544157} {:answer/id #uuid "36a59f0c-6350-5ee2-ab7b-1e2e0aaab216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544206} {:answer/id #uuid "8dd330f2-c63f-5936-b6a4-80ea6b670b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544392} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f468c2-e5f3-55da-b91c-73e467a1b0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544572} {:answer/id #uuid "e659aca7-3288-5e5d-8c4f-7e31771aa20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544581}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544572} :answer-field/id #uuid "87f1cabe-8e50-570a-a56a-29d676db3c4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9ce41098-082c-5659-8a15-6d5205341359" :question/math-academy-id "q-73747" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(-1,1,1)$, $B(2,-2,1)$, $C(1,2,2)$, and $D(2,-1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-2j+k)-(-i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-3j \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+2k)-(-i+j+k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i-j+4k)-(-i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(1\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 1)+3(2\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 1)+0 \\\\  & =15+9 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|24|=24.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ff80067a-229b-58c3-ad50-df0a4ac2c88f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544939}}] :activity/title "Volumes of Parallelepipeds" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544084}]}
